94:           "policy": "Each fisher must land at least one unit of fish per day; any surplus over one unit goes to a communal pot, and any shortfall is met by redistributing the pot's surplus equally, with second trips required until all meet the daily minimum.",
95:           "operationalization": "Daily routine: 1) All fishers land and record catch weight on the communal ledger board by signing their name. 2) The keeper (weekly voter-chosen, with a backup in the rotation list) tallies total surplus S = sum(max(catch-1,0)) and counts shortfall fishers n = number of fishers with catch<1. 3) If S>=n, give each shortfall fisher 1 unit from the pot; any leftover S-n stays in the pot for the next day. 4) If S<n, give each shortfall fisher S/n from the pot; any remaining shortfall fishers must perform a second trip that day to reach 1 unit. 5) The pot balance is updated by the keeper and posted beside the landing and announced during the brief. 6) Absences are logged as 0 catch and counted as shortfall; no penalty for a single day, but three consecutive absences constitute a repeated absence and trigger a penalty: the fisher must either catch the missing weight the next day or pay 1 unit into the pot. 7) Failure to return for a second trip after a shortfall, or refusal to record catch, is a violation: the council may order an immediate return, require a 0.5 unit penalty into the pot, or bar the fisher from fishing one day. 8) All violations are noted in the ledger, discussed at the weekly council meeting, and enforced by the village council. 9) The rotating keeper\u2019s schedule is written on the ledger at week start; if the appointed keeper is absent, the next in the rotation steps in. 10) The pot is physically stored in a communal box at the landing, and its contents are tracked solely by the ledger.",
