154:             "answer": "The rotating keeper of the village council (or a volunteer chosen by the council) will be the one who physically moves the fish from the communal box to the individual fishers.  After the daily tally is posted on the ledger, the keeper will count the surplus in the pot, then hand out equal portions to each fisher whose catch fell below 1 unit until every shortfall is covered, leaving every fisher with exactly one unit of fish.  The distribution is done in front of the others at the dock so that the ledger can be checked and the amounts verified.",
