166:             "answer": "As the keeper, I will count shortfall fishers by having each fisher write their name and catch weight on the ledger. After everyone has landed, I add up the total and check who is below 1 unit. Those are the shortfall fishers; I record the number n in the ledger under a column \u2018shortfall\u2019. I then compute the surplus S, and distribute S\u2011n as described. If a fisher still has less than 1 unit after the first distribution, I note that they are returning for a second trip and will update their entry once they return. This way, the ledger always shows who fell short, how much surplus was available, and how it was shared.",
167:             "revised_policy": "Everyone should fish once per day and aim to catch at least 1 unit of fish. If the catch is less than 1 unit, the fisher will go back for a second trip until they reach 1 unit. Any extra weight beyond 1 unit is set aside in a communal pot, which is kept at the communal landing. The pot is tracked by a simple ledger board where each fisher records the surplus weight. At the end of each day, the surplus fish are divided equally among the fishers who caught less than 1 unit that day. If the pot does not contain enough surplus to bring all shortfall fishers up to 1 unit, each shortfall fisher receives an equal share of what is available, and those still below 1 unit must return for another trip that same day to meet their daily requirement. Those who caught exactly 1 unit keep all of their catch. The communal pot is managed by the village council, with a rotating keeper each week. On each day, after all fishers have landed, tally total surplus S and count shortfall fishers n. If S \u2265 n, give each shortfall fisher 1 unit; any remaining surplus S\u2011n stays in the pot for the next day. If S < n, give each shortfall fisher S/n. Shortfall fishers who still have less than 1 unit will make a second trip that day. Record all transfers on the ledger. The pot remains for the next day.",
168:             "revised_operationalization": "Each fisher records their catch weight and whether they reached 1 unit on the ledger. The keeper tallies the total surplus S and counts the number of shortfall fishers n. The surplus is then distributed as per the policy: if S \u2265 n, each shortfall fisher receives 1 unit; if S < n, each receives S/n. Any remaining surplus stays in the pot for the next day. The ledger is updated with all transfers and any subsequent trips if shortfall fishers still need more fish."
