179:             "revised_policy": "Everyone should fish once per day and aim to catch at least 1 unit of fish. If the catch is less than 1 unit, the fisher will go back for a second trip until they reach 1 unit. Any extra weight beyond 1 unit is set aside in a communal pot, which is kept at the communal landing. The pot is tracked by a simple ledger board where each fisher records the surplus weight. At the end of each day, the surplus fish are divided equally among the fishers who caught less than 1 unit that day. If the pot does not contain enough surplus to bring all shortfall fishers up to 1 unit, each shortfall fisher receives an equal share of what is available, and those still below 1 unit must return for another trip that same day to meet their daily requirement. Those who caught exactly 1 unit keep all of their catch. The communal pot is managed by the village council, with a rotating keeper each week. On each day, after all fishers have landed, tally total surplus S and count shortfall fishers n. If S \u2265 n, give each shortfall fisher 1 unit; any remaining surplus S\u2011n stays in the pot for the next day. If S < n, give each shortfall fisher S/n. Shortfall fishers who still have less than 1 unit will make a second trip that day. Record all transfers on the ledger. The pot remains for the next day. Violation handling: If a fisher fails to return for a second trip after a shortfall, they are considered in breach. The council may order them to make the missed trip immediately, or to pay the shortfall into the pot as a penalty. Similarly, if a fisher refuses to record catch on the ledger, they are fined by having to provide an extra 0.5 unit to the pot or be barred from fishing for one day. All violations will be recorded in the ledger and discussed in the weekly council meeting.",
